<quiz>
<question type="stack">
  <name><text>How the error changes when the strips are halved</text></name>
  <questiontext format="html">
    <text><![CDATA[<p>Baraka estimated \(\displaystyle \int_{ {@lo@} }^{ {@hi@} } \left({@fx@}\right)dx\) with the trapezoidal rule. With \(2\) strips he got \(T_2 = {@exd(T2v)@}\), and with \(4\) strips \(T_4 = {@exd(T4v)@}\).</p><p>Take error \(=\) estimate \(-\) exact value (it may be negative). Give exact values; you may type fractions.</p><p>(a) Find the exact value of the integral.</p><div>Exact value \(=\) [[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]] [[feedback:prt1]]</div><p>(b) Find the error of \(T_2\).</p><div>Error of \(T_2 =\) [[input:ans2]] [[validation:ans2]] [[feedback:prt2]]</div><p>(c) Find the error of \(T_4\).</p><div>Error of \(T_4 =\) [[input:ans3]] [[validation:ans3]] [[feedback:prt3]]</div><p>(d) Use the pattern in the errors to predict \(T_8\), the estimate with \(8\) strips, without calculating it.</p><div>\(T_8 =\) [[input:ans4]] [[validation:ans4]] [[feedback:prt4]]</div>]]></text>
  </questiontext>
  <generalfeedback format="html">
    <text><![CDATA[<p>For a polynomial of degree up to \(3\), doubling the number of strips divides the error of the trapezoidal rule by \(4\), and the error keeps its sign.</p><p>(a) \(\displaystyle \int_{ {@lo@} }^{ {@hi@} } \left({@fx@}\right)dx = \left[{@Fx@}\right]_{ {@lo@} }^{ {@hi@} } = {@exd(Ex)@}\).</p><p>(b) Error of \(T_2 = {@exd(T2v)@} - {@exd(Ex)@} = {@exd(e2)@}\).</p><p>(c) Error of \(T_4 = {@exd(T4v)@} - {@exd(Ex)@} = {@exd(e4)@}\), a quarter of the error of \(T_2\).</p><p>(d) The error of \(T_8\) should be \({@exd(e4)@} \div 4 = {@e4/4@}\), so \(T_8 = {@exd(Ex)@} [[if test="is(e4>0)"]]+ {@e4/4@}[[else]]- {@-e4/4@}[[/if]] = {@T8v@}\), which is \({@float(T8v)@}\).</p>]]></text>
  </generalfeedback>
  <defaultgrade>4</defaultgrade>
  <penalty>0.1</penalty>
  <hidden>0</hidden>
